# Force LF line endings for all text files to ensure consistent behavior
# across platforms (prevents CRLF issues in golden tests on Windows)
* text=auto eol=lf
# Fuzz corpus entries are byte-exact inputs. Line-ending normalisation would
# silently rewrite them — and the CRLF seed exists precisely to prove CRLF
# survives, so normalising it turns the test into a tautology.
fuzz/corpus/** -text -diff

# Conformance cases and goldens are compared byte for byte, CRLF cases
# included: no line-ending conversion on any platform.
tests/jinja_conformance/cases/** -text
